# Commit hygiene

When the user asks to commit, **before** `git commit`:

1. Run `uv run ruff format .` and `uv run ruff check --fix .`.
2. Append a new entry to `ITERATION_LOG.md` (newest first).

Each log entry must include:

- Date (`YYYY-MM-DD`)
- Short title matching the change intent
- 1–3 bullets: what changed and why (not a file dump)
- Optional: commands to verify (`dbt test`, `dbt run`, etc.)

Stage the updated `ITERATION_LOG.md` with the same commit. Only update the log when committing — do not invent entries for commits the user did not ask for.
